Your two questions:
Q1 Is the 5(j) seam safe to ship? Yes, with one pin. `afterLstat`/`timeoutMs` (243-247) are in-process function/number parameters of an exported helper; nothing in argv, env, HTTP or StartServerOptions reaches them, and store.ts passes none. The sibling `RunVerifyOptions.afterRead` (10(h)) is the same shape as the existing `pipeline` option; `main.ts` passes no options. The stop condition at 787-789 already forbids making either reachable. Advisory A1: add a one-line source pin (a test that greps store.ts/main.ts for `afterLstat|afterRead|timeoutMs`) so the stop condition is enforced rather than prose.
Q2 Can any other live field hide a Needs-you card? No. Needs-you is derived only from `probationes` (cardRow board.ts:92-93; store needsYou) and petitiones, neither of which is overlaid now. `state` only moves the card between columns (a card with a pending human gate stays in needs_you whatever its state, board.ts:131), `heartbeat` is rendered nowhere (grep of apps/web, server, core), `traditio` reaches the page only as string rows in the drawer (board.ts:325-328). Row 6(f)/(g) pin both.

F8. MED (blocking; new, a hole in the own-tree rule at 102-109, row 10(d)/11(j)). The rule compares `rev-parse --show-toplevel` of `--repo` and of the studio, so `--repo` pointing at a SUBDIRECTORY of the same checkout (`verify W-X --studio studio --repo packages/cli`, or `ci --repo packages/cli`) passes. Probed: from a subdirectory `git ls-tree -r HEAD` lists only that subtree with relative paths, and sourceTreeHash (sourceTree.ts:44-58) hashes exactly that; commands also run with cwd = the subdirectory (pipeline index.ts:79). So a certificate over a partial tree plus a `review` state is written. Same class as --commit / ci --ref / --repo clone (4th instance; searched: --commit, --repo clone, --repo subdir, ci --ref, ci --repo, --studio-relative exclude path).
   Fix: add to the rule that `git -C <repo> rev-parse --show-prefix` is empty (equivalently realpath(repo) == realpath(toplevel)), still fail-closed on error. Rows: 10(d) and 11(j) gain `--repo <subdirectory of the checkout>`: gates written, state untouched, no events.

Advisories (non-blocking):
A1. See Q1: pin that the injections are unreachable from production callers.
A2. Admin-gitdir back-pointer and `.git` are both in builder-writable .git; the corroboration guards mistakes, not a hostile builder who edits both. The real bounds are the allowlist (state in 3 active states, traditio, heartbeat) and the committed base - which the brief states. No action.
A3. Clearing after 6 failures or a per-opus drop still mints reversal state_changed events (A3 residual) - accepted by the brief.
